From: Ning <hwn123123@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] aidl: match Android APN traffic descriptor and default rule

Use the APN as DNN, size its parcelable after serialization and allow the
default URSP rule for ordinary APN requests without an OS app id. Qualcomm
otherwise rejects data setup with MATCH_ALL_RULE_NOT_ALLOWED (2253). This
follows the Android DataProfileManager and DataNetwork request semantics.

diff --git a/src/binder_data.c b/src/binder_data.c
index c780c71..3ca4ecc 100644
--- a/src/binder_data.c
+++ b/src/binder_data.c
@@ -1697,2 +1697,5 @@ binder_data_call_setup_submit(
-        gbinder_writer_append_int32(&writer, 3 * sizeof(gint32));
-        gbinder_writer_append_string16(&writer, NULL); /* trafficDescriptor.dnn */
+        const gint32 descriptor_size = gbinder_writer_bytes_written(&writer);
+        gbinder_writer_append_int32(&writer, -1);
+        /* Match Android DataProfileManager: use this profile's APN as DNN.
+         * A present descriptor with neither DNN nor OS app id is invalid. */
+        gbinder_writer_append_string16(&writer, setup->apn);
@@ -1699,0 +1703,2 @@ binder_data_call_setup_submit(
+        gbinder_writer_overwrite_int32(&writer, descriptor_size,
+            gbinder_writer_bytes_written(&writer) - descriptor_size);
@@ -1712 +1717,3 @@ binder_data_call_setup_submit(
-        gbinder_writer_append_bool(&writer, FALSE); /* matchAllRuleAllowed */
+        /* Ordinary APN data has no OS app id; permit the modem's default
+         * URSP rule, matching Android's non-enterprise data request. */
+        gbinder_writer_append_bool(&writer, TRUE); /* matchAllRuleAllowed */
